1
00:03:09,563 --> 00:03:14,651
Someone invited me to this
cafe business conference next week.

2
00:03:14,651 --> 00:03:16,862
If you want, I'll just give you the invite.

3
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:19,782
It's at Claremont Hotel.

4
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,784
Sure, please.
Send me the details.

5
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,827
There's nothing special in what I did.

6
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:25,621
It's just bare minimum.

7
00:03:25,621 --> 00:03:27,998
I have no time to spare
on someone like you.

8
00:03:27,998 --> 00:03:29,833
Same old you.

9
00:03:30,584 --> 00:03:32,127
Non-believer of love.

10
00:03:32,586 --> 00:03:33,962
Lopez!

11
00:03:34,713 --> 00:03:36,757
I hate you! You jerk!

12
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:39,802
You deserved it.

13
00:03:40,636 --> 00:03:43,097
Why do you look like that?
You look sick.

14
00:03:43,722 --> 00:03:44,598
No, I'm fine.

15
00:03:44,598 --> 00:03:45,891
Stop crying!

16
00:03:45,891 --> 00:03:47,559
I said, stop.
You won't stop, huh?

17
00:03:47,559 --> 00:03:48,769
You won't stop?

18
00:03:48,852 --> 00:03:50,354
Enough!

19
00:03:51,605 --> 00:03:52,231
Kierra?

20
00:03:52,231 --> 00:03:53,273
You’re safe here.

21
00:03:53,273 --> 00:03:54,608
Kierra, you’re safe here

22
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:55,567
Okay?

23
00:03:55,651 --> 00:03:56,443
All right.

24
00:03:56,819 --> 00:03:58,487
I’ll take you out on a date.

25
00:03:59,321 --> 00:04:01,281
Let me make you a special drink,

26
00:04:02,199 --> 00:04:03,450
to switch things up.

27
00:04:05,327 --> 00:04:07,788
Fine. surprise me.

28
00:04:16,964 --> 00:04:18,048
You really like it, huh?

29
00:04:19,299 --> 00:04:22,261
Well, you won't find that anywhere else.

30
00:04:23,345 --> 00:04:25,556
That's why you have no choice
but to come back here.

31
00:04:26,890 --> 00:04:28,100
You fell into my trap.

32
00:04:30,477 --> 00:04:31,270
Whatever.

33
00:05:10,308 --> 00:05:11,309
See you yesterday.

34
00:05:12,841 --> 00:05:14,676
Yesterday’s already in the past.

35
00:05:14,771 --> 00:05:15,898
You should say,
“See you soon”.

36
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:20,986
By tomorrow, today
will just be another yesterday—

37
00:05:21,278 --> 00:05:23,739
and tomorrow will be another
yesterday, the next day.

38
00:05:24,239 --> 00:05:27,034
The past is certain,
the future is not.

39
00:05:28,202 --> 00:05:29,578
So, I'll see you certainly.

40
00:05:31,955 --> 00:05:33,248
That's what it means.

41
00:05:35,709 --> 00:05:36,877
See you yesterday.

42
00:05:37,544 --> 00:05:38,712
See you yesterday.

43
00:05:45,594 --> 00:05:46,970
Excuse me.

44
00:05:47,304 --> 00:05:48,472
Can I order now?

45
00:05:48,472 --> 00:05:50,849
Oh sure.
Sorry for the wait, ma'am.

46
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:56,313
Sorry ma'am, what's your order?

47
00:05:56,313 --> 00:05:57,898
- Okay, I'm having—
- Yeah…

48
00:05:57,898 --> 00:05:59,191
a caramel macchiato.

49
00:05:59,191 --> 00:05:59,983
Okay.

50
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:04,446
Also, one cheesecake.

51
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:09,535
So your order is—

52
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,203
- one caramel macchiato, iced.
- Yes.

53
00:06:11,203 --> 00:06:12,829
- And one cheesecake.
- And then—

54
00:06:18,043 --> 00:06:19,169
It's so hot!

55
00:06:19,878 --> 00:06:20,587
Hey, Ke!

56
00:06:21,463 --> 00:06:24,591
Hey, Theo! You're a lifesaver.

57
00:06:25,052 --> 00:06:26,595
It’s really hot today.

58
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,122
Why are you just covering me?

59
00:06:28,147 --> 00:06:30,315
- Cover yourself, too.
- No, it's fine. I'm okay.

60
00:06:30,764 --> 00:06:33,225
Really? You're sweating.
You might get sick.

61
00:06:33,225 --> 00:06:36,311
Geez.
You worry too much about me.

62
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:38,480
I might end up falling for you.

63
00:06:38,939 --> 00:06:40,899
You're crazy. Let's go.

64
00:06:42,822 --> 00:06:43,990
Almost there.

65
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:46,241
I'm almost going crazy for you.

66
00:08:23,043 --> 00:08:24,169
Can I help?

67
00:08:27,589 --> 00:08:28,507
Let me see.

68
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:40,477
There you go.

69
00:08:41,186 --> 00:08:43,438
It's a little better now.

70
00:08:43,772 --> 00:08:49,403
But we can fix it better
when we get home.

71
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:50,278
Thank you.

72
00:08:54,908 --> 00:08:55,784
Shan.

73
00:08:56,618 --> 00:09:01,415
Your mom told me you want
to go to high school in Manila?

74
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:05,585
Yes, but Mom doesn't want me to do it.

75
00:09:05,961 --> 00:09:09,214
She says it's better here.
Far away from Dad.

76
00:09:12,467 --> 00:09:14,553
But do you really want to study in Manila?

77
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:23,854
Okay, fine.

78
00:09:24,187 --> 00:09:26,189
I'll talk to your mom about this.

79
00:09:26,606 --> 00:09:27,941
You'll do that for me?

80
00:09:28,525 --> 00:09:29,276
Wait…

81
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:31,945
In exchange for what?

82
00:09:33,655 --> 00:09:34,448
Nothing.

83
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:38,243
I just want you to live the life you want.

84
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:40,746
You're like a son to me.

85
00:09:41,371 --> 00:09:42,706
You don't mean that.

86
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:48,336
I know you're finding it hard

87
00:09:48,336 --> 00:09:50,630
to accept me as part of your life.

88
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:57,345
But I'll keep trying until you accept me.

89
00:09:59,514 --> 00:10:01,558
I know what you've been through, Shan.

90
00:10:02,684 --> 00:10:06,688
And I think you've been
very brave through it all.

91
00:10:07,397 --> 00:10:12,569
Your mom is just worried about you
because you'll be alone in Manila.

92
00:10:12,944 --> 00:10:17,491
But if that's what you really want,
we'll find a way.

93
00:10:17,991 --> 00:10:18,700
Okay?

94
00:10:19,701 --> 00:10:21,828
Okay.
Thank you, Uncle.

95
00:10:24,122 --> 00:10:25,999
I promise to protect you and your mom.

96
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:28,752
Do you know why?

97
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,546
Because I love you both.

98
00:10:33,423 --> 00:10:37,761
If you have anything else to say,
I'm here. Okay?

99
00:10:38,845 --> 00:10:43,016
And if you want, we can go to other
beaches around here.

100
00:10:44,476 --> 00:10:46,353
Thank you, Uncle.

101
00:10:49,064 --> 00:10:50,857
<i>You’re a good kid, Shan.</i>

102
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:53,685
<i>A good kid, huh?</i>

103
00:10:54,615 --> 00:10:56,335
They used to tell me that all the time.

104
00:10:56,859 --> 00:11:00,154
<i>But... Am I still a good kid now?</i>

105
00:11:01,084 --> 00:11:02,084
I don't know.

106
00:11:06,055 --> 00:11:07,348
Yeah, I’ll follow.

107
00:11:15,928 --> 00:11:16,929
Shan.

108
00:11:16,929 --> 00:11:17,554
Bro.

109
00:11:17,554 --> 00:11:18,514
Bro.

110
00:11:18,514 --> 00:11:19,807
'Sup, homie.

111
00:11:20,474 --> 00:11:21,266
How are you?

112
00:11:23,227 --> 00:11:24,102
So…

113
00:11:24,728 --> 00:11:25,604
You thought about it?

114
00:11:26,355 --> 00:11:28,816
You really don't want to join?

115
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:31,151
- Frat?
- Mhmm.

116
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,110
No.

117
00:11:32,486 --> 00:11:33,362
Come on.

118
00:11:33,779 --> 00:11:34,947
Bro, just think about it.

119
00:11:34,947 --> 00:11:36,657
Just stop, stop.
Stop.

120
00:11:36,657 --> 00:11:38,951
Being a member of a fraternity
has many advantages.

121
00:11:39,201 --> 00:11:43,997
Most of our teachers are alumni
of the same fraternity. Remember?

122
00:11:44,164 --> 00:11:46,458
You never know when you
might need the right connections, and...

123
00:11:46,458 --> 00:11:47,167
think about it.

124
00:11:47,876 --> 00:11:50,128
After the bar, you'll get a job.

125
00:11:50,462 --> 00:11:52,256
It's very different when you
have someone backing you up.

126
00:11:54,925 --> 00:11:57,845
So, nepotism? Corruption?

127
00:11:58,637 --> 00:12:01,640
Funny, isn't it?
It's no big deal to you.

128
00:12:02,099 --> 00:12:03,308
Oh, Shan…

129
00:12:03,308 --> 00:12:06,311
I didn't create the system.
It's already there.

130
00:12:06,311 --> 00:12:07,771
Bro, it has been around for a long time.

131
00:12:07,771 --> 00:12:09,690
I'm just here for the long game.

132
00:12:12,693 --> 00:12:15,237
Haze, do you know anyone named Miguel?

133
00:12:16,321 --> 00:12:17,072
Which one?

134
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:22,160
Delos Santos, Madahan,
Reyes, Lumpas…

135
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,620
There are many Miguels in my circle.

136
00:12:24,496 --> 00:12:25,539
Villaflor.

137
00:12:27,374 --> 00:12:29,501
Why? Is he still out there?

138
00:12:30,711 --> 00:12:31,461
What do you mean?

139
00:12:32,546 --> 00:12:33,839
Is he supposed to be in jail?

140
00:12:34,172 --> 00:12:35,215
Shouldn’t he be?

141
00:12:35,299 --> 00:12:37,718
He has a history of
drugging people at parties.

142
00:12:38,135 --> 00:12:41,388
Someone also filed a lawsuit,
but it was dismissed for some reason.

143
00:12:42,306 --> 00:12:45,642
For "some reason"—
referring to his father.

144
00:12:46,226 --> 00:12:49,062
Wait, wait. Villaflor, right?

145
00:12:49,189 --> 00:12:51,442
So this is the mayor's son?

146
00:12:52,107 --> 00:12:53,010
Yes.

147
00:12:53,150 --> 00:12:56,653
His grandfather is a senator,
and his uncles are in the government.

148
00:12:57,070 --> 00:12:57,846
Fuck.

149
00:12:58,405 --> 00:13:00,532
They have turned
the government into a business.

150
00:13:00,991 --> 00:13:01,955
Right?

151
00:13:02,034 --> 00:13:04,578
They will not allow their
name to be tarnished.

152
00:13:05,078 --> 00:13:06,163
That is why they will do
everything possible

153
00:13:06,163 --> 00:13:08,040
to cover up Miguel's shit.

154
00:13:09,541 --> 00:13:11,418
He is violent and also has a huge ego.

155
00:13:11,919 --> 00:13:13,921
He thinks he is superior to everyone else.

156
00:13:16,590 --> 00:13:17,549
Come on, Shan.

157
00:13:17,883 --> 00:13:20,719
I know you want to.
Just give it a chance.

158
00:13:20,969 --> 00:13:21,887
You won't regret it.

159
00:13:21,887 --> 00:13:23,513
You never take "no" for an answer, do you?

160
00:13:24,056 --> 00:13:24,863
Can you?

161
00:13:30,771 --> 00:13:32,773
Okay. Sure.

162
00:13:32,952 --> 00:13:33,744
You’re right.

163
00:13:34,168 --> 00:13:36,318
I'll give you some space
so you don't get mad at me.

164
00:13:36,568 --> 00:13:37,110
But—

165
00:13:37,694 --> 00:13:39,154
Shan, bro.

166
00:13:40,053 --> 00:13:43,265
I’m telling you this is an opportunity, and
you know why?

167
00:13:46,119 --> 00:13:47,496
You fit in with us.

168
00:14:01,051 --> 00:14:03,011
<i>Shan, I miss you!</i>

169
00:14:03,428 --> 00:14:05,097
<i>When can I see you? </i>

170
00:14:05,389 --> 00:14:07,057
<i>Don't forget the books, okay?</i>

171
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,394
Here you go.

172
00:14:12,419 --> 00:14:13,712
And something for you, too.

173
00:14:13,821 --> 00:14:14,822
Thanks, Shan.

174
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:18,110
But next time,
let's just meet at the cafe, okay?

175
00:14:18,388 --> 00:14:19,932
I'll let Roel know, too.

176
00:14:20,570 --> 00:14:23,156
Relax. I heard Dad isn't even home.

177
00:14:23,156 --> 00:14:24,866
I heard he's going to Osaka.

178
00:14:26,535 --> 00:14:28,787
You know, if you
weren't here in this house,

179
00:14:29,788 --> 00:14:30,872
I wouldn't keep coming.

180
00:14:30,872 --> 00:14:32,124
I won't come here often.

181
00:14:32,879 --> 00:14:34,042
What’s that for anyway?

182
00:14:35,043 --> 00:14:35,711
Shan.

183
00:14:39,631 --> 00:14:41,049
Elyse, go to your room.

184
00:14:59,192 --> 00:14:59,985
Fuck you.

185
00:14:59,985 --> 00:15:01,987
Were you hiding your
mother's money from me?

186
00:15:02,461 --> 00:15:03,332
Huh?

187
00:15:03,613 --> 00:15:04,614
Why?

188
00:15:05,365 --> 00:15:06,867
You wanna take that too?

189
00:15:07,075 --> 00:15:07,743
Huh?

190
00:15:09,244 --> 00:15:11,747
How dare you talk back to me?
Damn you!

191
00:15:13,915 --> 00:15:14,916
What?

192
00:15:15,751 --> 00:15:17,377
Do you want her money too?

193
00:15:17,502 --> 00:15:18,170
Huh?

194
00:15:18,170 --> 00:15:20,297
Are you angry because
she didn't leave you anything?

195
00:15:20,547 --> 00:15:25,343
After everything you left her with— all the
problems, the trauma, the pain, the wounds.

196
00:15:25,552 --> 00:15:27,095
And what? A secret family?

197
00:15:27,095 --> 00:15:28,096
Fuck you.

198
00:15:28,330 --> 00:15:30,207
Don't even think about
involving Elyse in this.

199
00:15:32,559 --> 00:15:34,352
Don't get me fucking wrong.

200
00:15:35,562 --> 00:15:37,272
Elyse has nothing to do with this.

201
00:15:37,626 --> 00:15:38,877
This is all you.

202
00:15:40,233 --> 00:15:41,651
This is all you!

203
00:15:42,027 --> 00:15:42,861
What's this?

204
00:15:44,196 --> 00:15:44,988
What is this?

205
00:15:46,031 --> 00:15:47,866
Do you want to take revenge on me?

206
00:15:48,424 --> 00:15:49,926
Well? Go ahead!

207
00:15:49,951 --> 00:15:52,162
Tighter.
Do you want to kill me?

208
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:53,894
Can you?

209
00:15:54,122 --> 00:15:54,915
Go ahead.

210
00:15:54,946 --> 00:15:55,932
Why?

211
00:15:55,957 --> 00:15:57,584
Do you want to die?

212
00:15:57,793 --> 00:16:00,879
Doesn't it seem too easy to you, Dad?

213
00:16:01,963 --> 00:16:02,756
Huh?

214
00:16:06,304 --> 00:16:08,598
Go ahead. Can you do it?

215
00:16:10,097 --> 00:16:11,098
Go.

216
00:16:14,684 --> 00:16:15,644
Kill me.

217
00:16:18,772 --> 00:16:21,024
So I could be just like your mom.

218
00:16:22,499 --> 00:16:24,626
Your mom who's dead already.

219
00:16:32,702 --> 00:16:33,995
Fuck you.

220
00:16:38,075 --> 00:16:40,911
You're just like me.

221
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,846
Ciandrei! That's enough.

222
00:17:04,526 --> 00:17:06,278
Sir, let's go.

223
00:17:17,038 --> 00:17:19,249
<i>I was afraid of monsters growing up.</i>

224
00:17:21,209 --> 00:17:23,420
I tried to be brave to fight against them.

225
00:17:32,637 --> 00:17:34,472
But sometimes I wonder,

226
00:17:36,016 --> 00:17:37,267
What if…

227
00:17:39,769 --> 00:17:42,189
What if there's a little monster
inside of me, too?

228
00:17:43,273 --> 00:17:44,566
I’m not like him.

229
00:17:47,652 --> 00:17:49,112
I’m not like him.

230
00:17:55,994 --> 00:17:57,746
I don't want to be like them.

231
00:18:21,394 --> 00:18:23,438
Thank you. We’ll have your drinks ready
in a bit.

232
00:18:32,030 --> 00:18:32,989
What's that?

233
00:18:34,259 --> 00:18:37,346
Interior design for a coffee shop.
Isn’t it obvious?

234
00:18:44,597 --> 00:18:46,765
No outside drinks allowed here.

235
00:18:47,003 --> 00:18:50,715
But I'm not drinking it.
Just let me be, Ciandrei.

236
00:18:52,946 --> 00:18:55,866
Just call me Shan.
We're friends already, right?

237
00:18:57,013 --> 00:18:58,598
I don't want us to be friends.

238
00:18:59,828 --> 00:19:01,121
More than friends?

239
00:19:01,685 --> 00:19:02,684
Less.

240
00:19:04,396 --> 00:19:07,691
More than friends, less than lovers.

241
00:19:08,525 --> 00:19:10,860
All right, that sounds good to me.

242
00:19:17,215 --> 00:19:20,954
Ugh. No outside food allowed.

243
00:19:20,954 --> 00:19:24,124
You notice everything.
Do you have a problem?

244
00:19:24,945 --> 00:19:25,862
With you?

245
00:19:26,876 --> 00:19:27,836
No.

246
00:19:27,836 --> 00:19:29,212
No, with something else.

247
00:19:29,212 --> 00:19:31,589
Because it looks like
you're just distracting yourself.

248
00:19:37,137 --> 00:19:38,054
What is that?

249
00:19:38,805 --> 00:19:39,848
Is it because of that?

250
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:41,221
No.

251
00:19:41,246 --> 00:19:42,044
No, no.

252
00:19:42,517 --> 00:19:43,435
Just had a fight.

253
00:19:44,019 --> 00:19:44,936
It's nothing serious.

254
00:19:45,395 --> 00:19:46,813
Did a girl hit you?

255
00:19:49,107 --> 00:19:50,025
No.

256
00:19:56,418 --> 00:19:57,878
Hey, are you okay?

257
00:19:59,159 --> 00:20:00,827
Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

258
00:20:01,234 --> 00:20:03,110
Do you want my special Sakura drink?

259
00:20:05,457 --> 00:20:06,416
Okay.

260
00:20:07,042 --> 00:20:07,917
One order.

261
00:20:08,293 --> 00:20:11,421
All right. One Sakura drink for Kierra,
coming right up.

262
00:20:25,310 --> 00:20:26,978
<i>You want to get revenge on me?</i>

263
00:20:28,313 --> 00:20:29,981
Go ahead. Tighter.

264
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:31,524
You want to kill me?

265
00:20:36,446 --> 00:20:37,364
<i>Can you?</i>

266
00:20:37,864 --> 00:20:38,573
<i>Go ahead.</i>

267
00:20:38,573 --> 00:20:39,115
Why?

268
00:20:39,115 --> 00:20:40,950
Do you want to die?

269
00:20:41,076 --> 00:20:42,744
Isn't that too easy for you?

270
00:20:46,122 --> 00:20:46,790
<i>Go ahead.</i>

271
00:20:47,374 --> 00:20:48,333
Can you do it?

272
00:20:48,833 --> 00:20:49,626
Kill me.

273
00:20:49,626 --> 00:20:53,046
Kill me.

274
